# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hybrid Mode: GUPANUPAN2026 — Next.js builder with Puter + Totalum
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo is now HYBRID: Next.js UI from ai-app-builder-open + Puter.js backend
# Original Puter Vite builder is backed up in .puter-legacy/ (git history also has it)
# You can run in EITHER mode — or both:

# --- Option A: Puter (keyless, no env needed) ---
# Just run `npm run dev` — Puter.js loads from https://js.puter.com/v2/
# User signs in with Puter account, AI/storage/hosting all via puter.js.
# No TOTALUM_VCAAS_API_KEY required. Leave it empty and builder will show
# "Puter Ready" banner and store projects via puter.kv / puter.fs.

# --- Option B: Totalum (one API key, hosted sandboxes) ---
# Register at https://www.totalum.app/api → onboarding → "Use the Totalum API"
# API reference: https://www.totalum.app/totalum-api.md
TOTALUM_VCAAS_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public base URL. Used by src/proxy.ts to allow-list origin for CSP/CORS in prod.
# Defaults to same-host if unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-domain.com

# Force-enable Puter even if Totalum key is set (default: auto)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PUTER_ENABLED=1
